  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Best effort in words. The previous hours list was Dinka numerals (tök, rou, diäk, dhorou, thiäär), not Nuer; replaced with Nuer numerals (kɛl, rɛw, diɔk, ŋuaan, dhieec, bäkɛl, bäärɔw, bädäk, bäŋuan, wäl, wäl wi̱ kɛl, wäl wi̱ rɛw). Patterns 'thaar {h}' (the file's own hour word) + 'kɛnɛ minit <n>' (kɛnɛ = and/with; minit from the file), tens as jiɛn rɛw/diɔk/ŋuaan/dhieec with 'wi̱ dhieec' for +5; :30 written as thirty minutes because I do not trust the file's half word 'ku kel' (looks Dinka). Specific doubts: whether 'thaar' or 'thaak' is the Nuer clock word, the exact tens forms (jiɛn + n), the 11/12 forms with 'wi̱', and whether a quarter/half idiom exists. Much of the nus file (cäŋ, ruɔ̈n, thiäär, 'ku kel') looks Dinka-derived and deserves native review beyond this batch."
    }
  ]
